            <div xml:id="d224">

                <pb facs="0503" n="377" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg377"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.3515/1613: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Arica</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Von Tresckow</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Extract—Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Arica</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-09-13T12:00:00-04:42"><hi rendition="#italic">September 13,
                                1925—noon</hi>.</date><lb/>[Received September 14—10:45
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>From Pershing:</p>
                <p rendition="#center">. . . . . . . . . . . . . .</p>
                <p>In view of all that has taken place since my cable to you of August 6, I wish to
                    withdraw my suggestion that you make representations <pb facs="0504" n="378"
                        xml:id="pg378"/> to Presidents of Chile and Peru. I deem this action
                    inadvisable at the present time. I deeply appreciate tone of your cable which is
                    most gratifying. Edwards will return to Arica on Tuesday, and some improvement
                    in situation may be brought about by his return. I think it best for you not to
                    take action until later on, when occasion will probably arise as a result of our
                    demands for creation of essential prerequisites to free plebiscite. I shall
                    cable you later on. Pershing.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Von Tresckow</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
